From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:37:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a library's vertex shader
 compiled on its own

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl, a vertex shader alone in its pipeline
library (DXVK's pre-rasterization library) is now also compiled on its
own when the library is created, and its Metal library is built then,
on the application's thread (kk_gpl_compile_vertex). Its MSL depends on
no other library:

- Attributes are fetched through a layout the draw gives
  (kk_nir_lower_vbo_runtime): kk_flush_dynamic_state uploads one struct
  kk_vertex_fetch per attribute slot (format class, stride, divisor,
  input rate) from the dynamic vertex input state, and the new last
  field kk_per_draw_data::vertex_fetch points at it. The format word
  covers every format KosmicKrisp advertises for vertex buffers: 8, 16
  and 32-bit channels, 10-10-10-2 and 11-11-10, with the format's
  swizzle. The base address and robustness clamp stay in the root
  table, as for other vertex shaders. The root table's layout does not
  change, so no other shader's MSL does; per-draw data is uploaded
  without the new field unless the bound vertex shader reads it.
- It always writes a point size; the topology class is set on the Metal
  pipeline at link time.
- Its user varyings, and those of the fragment shader linked to it, are
  declared as vec4s (nir_to_msl_options::vec4_user_varyings), so that
  stages compiled apart agree however many components each uses.

The first draw of a fast link with that vertex shader compiles only the
fragment shader, reading 0 for what the vertex shader does not write,
and builds the pipeline with the vertex library already built
(kk_gpl_link_separate). The device link cache keys such links without
the vertex input state and with the topology's class only, so other
vertex layouts reuse the pipeline. A link the vertex shader cannot
serve compiles the whole pipeline as before, and [kk-compile] link
lines count the reasons: tessellation or geometry stages, transform
feedback, VK_POLYGON_MODE_POINT on triangles, another view mask, an
attribute format outside the fetch, a fragment input of another type
than the output, an indirectly indexed varying, a fragment shader
reading clip or cull distances. Pipelines that are not fast links,
link-time-optimized ones included, and everything without the flag
compile as before, to the same MSL.

The fragment side still compiles at the first draw; building it at
library creation too follows.

Linear: PLA-424
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-kk-gpl-host.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
